# luafan2/.dockerignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trim the docker build context so `docker build` doesn't ship the
# entire test tree, coverage artefacts, and CI caches to the daemon.
# Anything listed here is NOT sent as part of `docker build .` context,
# and therefore cannot be COPY'd into any stage.
#
# Kept (implicitly): CMakeLists.txt, src/, lua/, README.md, .luacov,
# and every top-level file the Release build needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build outputs
build/
build-asan/
build-coverage/
build-*/

# NOTE: DO NOT ignore tests/ here even though the release images do
# not COPY from it — .dockerignore is per-context, and CI builds
# tests/Dockerfile from the SAME context. That Dockerfile
# `COPY tests/docker-entrypoint.sh ...`, so hiding tests/ breaks CI.
# The release Dockerfiles simply don't COPY tests/, which costs a
# few KB of context upload but nothing more.

# Manifest, docs, and CI config — image content, not runtime code.
manifest/
docs/
.github/

# VCS + local scratch
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
tmp/

# Editor / OS turd
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
